  "question": {
    "text": "A body $A$ of mass $M$ while falling vertically downwards under gravity breaks into two parts; a body B of mass $1 / 3 \\mathrm{M}$ and a body $\\mathrm{C}$ of mass $2 / 3 \\mathrm{M}$. The centre of mass of bodies $\\mathrm{B}$ and $\\mathrm{C}$ taken together shifts compared to that of body $\\mathrm{A}$ towards",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gk41H",
      "text": "\ndepends on height of breaking\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GQp8R",
      "text": "\ndoes not shift\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "TaWNn",
      "text": "\nbody C\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "mllI0",
      "text": "\nbody B",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "No horizontal external force is acting\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{cm}}=0 \\\\\n& \\text { since } \\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{cm}}=0 \\\\\n& \\therefore \\Delta \\mathrm{x}_{\\mathrm{cm}}=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
